1
00:00:02,550 --> 00:00:03,968
KATARA: Water...

2
00:00:04,844 --> 00:00:06,012
Earth...

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:08,139
Fire...

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:10,183
Air.

5
00:00:11,017 --> 00:00:14,771
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,438 --> 00:00:18,525
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,484 --> 00:00:22,153
Only the Avatar,
master of all 4 elements,

8
00:00:22,278 --> 00:00:23,446
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,571 --> 00:00:25,573
But when the world
needed him most,

10
00:00:25,698 --> 00:00:26,824
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,242 --> 00:00:28,326
100 years passed,

12
00:00:28,409 --> 00:00:30,912
And my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar―

13
00:00:30,995 --> 00:00:32,539
An airbender named Aang.

14
00:00:32,914 --> 00:00:35,041
And although his airbending
skills are great,

15
00:00:35,124 --> 00:00:37,710
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

16
00:00:37,794 --> 00:00:38,795
AANG: Oof!

17
00:00:38,878 --> 00:00:41,673
KATARA: But I believe Aang
can save the world.

18
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:58,568
SOKKA: You guys
are gonna be done soon, right?

19
00:00:58,652 --> 00:01:02,113
We've got a lot of ground to cover
If we want to make it to Omashu today.

20
00:01:02,197 --> 00:01:04,908
What, like you're ready
to go right now, naked guy?

21
00:01:05,033 --> 00:01:06,743
I could be ready in two minutes.

22
00:01:06,826 --> 00:01:08,245
Seriously. Whenever.

23
00:01:08,370 --> 00:01:11,081
So, you were showing me
the octopus form.

24
00:01:11,206 --> 00:01:12,958
Right. Let me see your stance.

25
00:01:16,836 --> 00:01:18,213
Your arms are too far apart.

26
00:01:18,296 --> 00:01:21,258
See, if you move them
closer together, you protect your center.

27
00:01:21,341 --> 00:01:23,426
- You got it?
- Oh. Yeah.

28
00:01:23,510 --> 00:01:24,511
Thanks.

29
00:01:26,054 --> 00:01:27,430
Ok, let's see what you got.

30
00:01:45,448 --> 00:01:48,326
You make a fine octopus, pupil Aang.

31
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:51,955
( SPLASH )

32
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,207
( MUSIC PLAYING )

33
00:01:54,666 --> 00:01:56,751
( MAN HUMMING )

34
00:01:56,918 --> 00:01:58,003
♪ Don't fall in love

35
00:01:58,086 --> 00:02:00,130
♪ With a traveling girl

36
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:01,881
♪ She'll leave you broke

37
00:02:01,965 --> 00:02:04,134
♪ And broken-hearted

38
00:02:04,217 --> 00:02:05,802
( MUSIC STOPS )

39
00:02:05,927 --> 00:02:07,512
Hey, hey! River people.

40
00:02:08,054 --> 00:02:09,222
We're not river people.

41
00:02:09,764 --> 00:02:10,849
You're not?

42
00:02:10,932 --> 00:02:12,892
Well, then what kind
of people are you?

43
00:02:12,976 --> 00:02:14,477
Just people.

44
00:02:14,853 --> 00:02:17,147
Aren't we all, brother? Hoo!

45
00:02:17,230 --> 00:02:18,398
Who are you?

46
00:02:18,481 --> 00:02:19,482
I'm Chong.

47
00:02:19,566 --> 00:02:20,942
And this is my wife, Lily.

48
00:02:21,026 --> 00:02:22,110
We're nomads.

49
00:02:22,193 --> 00:02:24,612
Happy to go wherever
the wind takes us.

50
00:02:24,696 --> 00:02:25,780
( SINGS GIBBERISH )

51
00:02:26,239 --> 00:02:27,490
You guys are nomads?!

52
00:02:27,574 --> 00:02:29,617
That's great! I'm a nomad!

53
00:02:29,993 --> 00:02:31,494
Hey! Me, too!

54
00:02:31,911 --> 00:02:33,079
I know.

55
00:02:33,163 --> 00:02:34,247
You just said that.

56
00:02:34,331 --> 00:02:37,417
Oh. Nice underwear.

57
00:02:40,170 --> 00:02:42,088
( GASPS )

58
00:02:43,631 --> 00:02:44,716
( GRUNTING )

59
00:02:44,799 --> 00:02:46,468
I didn't find anything to eat.

60
00:02:46,551 --> 00:02:48,136
I can't live like this.

61
00:02:48,219 --> 00:02:49,971
I wasn't meant to be a fugitive.

62
00:02:50,055 --> 00:02:51,639
This is impossible!

63
00:02:52,182 --> 00:02:53,183
Uncle...

64
00:02:53,266 --> 00:02:54,642
What are you doing?

65
00:02:55,310 --> 00:02:57,979
You're looking at
the rare white dragon bush.

66
00:02:58,104 --> 00:03:03,193
Its leaves make a tea
so delicious it's heartbreaking.

67
00:03:03,318 --> 00:03:06,363
That, or it's the white jade bush,

68
00:03:06,446 --> 00:03:08,031
which is poisonous.

69
00:03:08,531 --> 00:03:10,283
We need food, not tea.

70
00:03:10,367 --> 00:03:12,035
I'm going fishing.

71
00:03:12,118 --> 00:03:14,496
Hmm. Delectable tea,

72
00:03:14,579 --> 00:03:16,373
or deadly poison?

73
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:20,335
( LOWING )

74
00:03:21,711 --> 00:03:24,506
AANG: Hey, Sokka,
You should hear some of these stories.

75
00:03:24,756 --> 00:03:26,549
These guys have
been everywhere.

76
00:03:26,633 --> 00:03:29,094
Well, not everywhere,
little arrowhead,

77
00:03:29,177 --> 00:03:30,762
but where we haven't been,

78
00:03:30,845 --> 00:03:33,390
we've heard about
through stories and songs.

79
00:03:34,307 --> 00:03:36,976
They said they'll take us to see
a giant night crawler.

80
00:03:37,060 --> 00:03:41,773
MOKU: On the way, there's a waterfall
that creates a never-ending rainbow!

81
00:03:41,898 --> 00:03:43,775
Look, I hate to be
the wet blanket here,

82
00:03:43,858 --> 00:03:46,319
but since Katara is busy,
I guess it's up to me.

83
00:03:46,694 --> 00:03:48,196
We need to get to Omashu.

84
00:03:48,321 --> 00:03:52,033
No sidetracks, no worms,
and definitely no rainbows.

85
00:03:52,909 --> 00:03:57,330
Whoa! Sounds like someone's
got a case of destination fever.

86
00:03:57,414 --> 00:03:58,456
( LAUGHS )

87
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:00,834
You're worried too much about
where you're going.

88
00:04:01,126 --> 00:04:03,294
LILY: You gotta focus
less on the where

89
00:04:03,378 --> 00:04:04,879
and more on the going.

90
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:06,423
Oh...

91
00:04:06,506 --> 00:04:07,590
Ma...

92
00:04:07,674 --> 00:04:08,675
Shu!

93
00:04:09,092 --> 00:04:10,093
Sokka's right.

94
00:04:10,176 --> 00:04:13,680
We need to find King Bumi so Aang
can learn earthbending somewhere safe.

95
00:04:13,763 --> 00:04:15,723
Well, sounds like you're
headed to Omashu.

96
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:19,436
There's an old story
about a secret pass...

97
00:04:19,978 --> 00:04:22,814
Right through the mountains.

98
00:04:23,565 --> 00:04:25,400
Is this real or a legend?

99
00:04:25,483 --> 00:04:27,235
Oh, it's a real legend.

100
00:04:27,318 --> 00:04:30,113
And it's as old as earthbending itself.

101
00:04:30,488 --> 00:04:32,031
( STRUMMING )

102
00:04:32,115 --> 00:04:33,158
( HUMMING )

103
00:04:33,241 --> 00:04:34,868
♪ Two lovers

104
00:04:34,951 --> 00:04:37,412
♪ Forbidden from one another

105
00:04:37,495 --> 00:04:42,333
♪ A war divides their people

106
00:04:42,417 --> 00:04:46,588
♪ And a mountain divides them apart

107
00:04:48,214 --> 00:04:53,636
♪ Built a path to be together ♪

108
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:55,763
Yeah, I forget the next couple lines,

109
00:04:55,847 --> 00:04:57,265
but then it goes...

110
00:04:57,348 --> 00:04:59,517
♪ Secret tunnel

111
00:04:59,601 --> 00:05:02,437
♪ Secret tunnel

112
00:05:02,562 --> 00:05:04,731
♪ Through the mountain

113
00:05:04,814 --> 00:05:09,068
♪ Secret, secret, secret, secret tunnel

114
00:05:09,152 --> 00:05:10,153
♪ Yeah ♪

115
00:05:10,236 --> 00:05:11,654
( APPLAUSE )

116
00:05:11,738 --> 00:05:13,698
I think we'll just
stick with flying.

117
00:05:13,781 --> 00:05:16,117
We've dealt with the Fire Nation before.

118
00:05:16,201 --> 00:05:17,285
We'll be fine.

119
00:05:17,368 --> 00:05:20,413
Yeah, thanks for the help,
but Appa hates going underground.

120
00:05:20,497 --> 00:05:23,082
And we need to do
whatever makes Appa most comfortable.

121
00:05:23,166 --> 00:05:24,167
( LOWING )

122
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:25,251
Launch!

123
00:05:25,335 --> 00:05:27,253
( SNARLING )

124
00:05:29,255 --> 00:05:31,007
( SCREAMING )

125
00:05:31,966 --> 00:05:34,010
Secret love cave. Let's go.

126
00:05:42,644 --> 00:05:46,105
IROH: Zuko, remember that plant
I thought might be tea?

127
00:05:46,564 --> 00:05:47,899
You didn't.

128
00:05:47,982 --> 00:05:49,275
I did.

129
00:05:49,359 --> 00:05:50,777
And it wasn't.

130
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:51,986
Aagh!

131
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,322
When the rash spreads
to my throat,

132
00:05:54,405 --> 00:05:56,074
I will stop breathing.

133
00:05:56,157 --> 00:05:57,700
But look what I found!

134
00:05:58,117 --> 00:05:59,786
These are pakui berries.

135
00:05:59,869 --> 00:06:03,164
Known to cure the poison
of the white jade plant!

136
00:06:03,748 --> 00:06:07,502
That, or makaola berries,
that cause blindness.

137
00:06:07,877 --> 00:06:10,463
We're not taking any more chances
with these plants!

138
00:06:10,547 --> 00:06:12,048
We need to get help.

139
00:06:12,131 --> 00:06:13,925
But where are we going to go?

140
00:06:14,467 --> 00:06:16,719
We're enemies of the Earth Kingdom,

141
00:06:16,803 --> 00:06:19,556
and fugitives from the Fire Nation.

142
00:06:20,890 --> 00:06:22,517
If the Earth Kingdom discovers us,

143
00:06:22,642 --> 00:06:24,269
they'll have us killed.

144
00:06:24,352 --> 00:06:26,604
But if the Fire Nation discovers us,

145
00:06:26,688 --> 00:06:28,690
We'll be turned over to Azula.

146
00:06:30,275 --> 00:06:31,901
Earth kingdom it is.

147
00:06:32,819 --> 00:06:34,779
SOKKA: How far are we
from the tunnel?

148
00:06:34,862 --> 00:06:36,864
Actually, it's not just one tunnel.

149
00:06:36,948 --> 00:06:40,243
The lovers didn't want anyone
to find out about their love,

150
00:06:40,326 --> 00:06:42,453
so they built a whole labyrinth.

151
00:06:43,204 --> 00:06:44,664
Labyrinth?!

152
00:06:44,747 --> 00:06:46,249
I'm sure we'll figure it out.

153
00:06:48,251 --> 00:06:51,087
All you need to
do is trust in love,

154
00:06:51,170 --> 00:06:53,131
according to the curse.

155
00:06:56,634 --> 00:06:57,635
( GROWLS )

156
00:06:57,719 --> 00:06:58,761
Curse?!

157
00:07:00,263 --> 00:07:02,098
CHONG: Hey, hey! We're here!

158
00:07:02,515 --> 00:07:04,517
SOKKA: What exactly is this curse?

159
00:07:05,143 --> 00:07:07,812
The curse says that only
those that trust in love

160
00:07:07,895 --> 00:07:09,689
can make it through the caves.

161
00:07:09,772 --> 00:07:11,899
Otherwise, you'll be
trapped in them forever.

162
00:07:11,983 --> 00:07:13,026
And die.

163
00:07:13,651 --> 00:07:15,194
Oh, yeah, and die.

164
00:07:15,903 --> 00:07:16,946
Hey!

165
00:07:17,030 --> 00:07:18,906
I just remembered
the rest of that song.

166
00:07:19,365 --> 00:07:22,243
( STRUMS ) ♪ And die ♪

167
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:26,164
That's it! There's no way
we're going through some cursed hole!

168
00:07:27,332 --> 00:07:30,877
Hey! Someone's making a big campfire!

169
00:07:31,294 --> 00:07:33,338
That's no campfire, Moku.

170
00:07:33,421 --> 00:07:34,547
It's Fire Nation.

171
00:07:34,631 --> 00:07:35,923
They're tracking us.

172
00:07:36,674 --> 00:07:39,677
So, all you need is to trust in love
to get through these caves?

173
00:07:39,761 --> 00:07:42,138
That is correct,
Master Arrowhead.

174
00:07:48,144 --> 00:07:49,312
We can make it.

175
00:07:49,395 --> 00:07:50,772
Everyone into the hole.

176
00:07:53,191 --> 00:07:55,068
( SNARLS )

177
00:08:01,574 --> 00:08:02,575
SOLDIER: Hold on!

178
00:08:02,659 --> 00:08:03,701
It's too dangerous.

179
00:08:04,035 --> 00:08:05,953
Haven't you heard the song?

180
00:08:06,037 --> 00:08:07,622
Just close them in.

181
00:08:07,705 --> 00:08:09,916
The mountain will take care of the rest.

182
00:08:25,765 --> 00:08:27,684
( GROWLING )

183
00:08:28,309 --> 00:08:30,436
KATARA: It's ok, Appa. We'll be fine.

184
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:31,688
I hope.

185
00:08:31,979 --> 00:08:33,523
We will be fine.

186
00:08:33,606 --> 00:08:34,857
All we need
is a plan.

187
00:08:34,941 --> 00:08:36,776
Chong, how long do those torches last?

188
00:08:36,859 --> 00:08:38,528
Um, about two hours each.

189
00:08:39,278 --> 00:08:42,365
And we have five torches,
so that's 10 hours.

190
00:08:42,448 --> 00:08:45,785
It doesn't work like that
if they're all lit at the same time!

191
00:08:45,868 --> 00:08:47,578
Oh! Right.

192
00:08:47,662 --> 00:08:50,957
I'm gonna make a map
to keep track of exactly where we've been.

193
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:54,836
Then we should be able to
solve it like a maze and get through.

194
00:08:56,963 --> 00:08:58,840
( APPA GROWLS )

195
00:09:03,845 --> 00:09:06,180
WOMAN: You two must not
be from around here.

196
00:09:06,264 --> 00:09:08,683
We know better
than to touch the white jade.

197
00:09:08,766 --> 00:09:11,436
Much less make it into tea and drink it.

198
00:09:12,019 --> 00:09:13,229
( LAUGHS ) Oops!

199
00:09:14,147 --> 00:09:17,066
- So, where are you traveling from?
- Yes, we're travelers.

200
00:09:17,442 --> 00:09:18,943
Do you have names?

201
00:09:19,026 --> 00:09:20,361
Names?

202
00:09:20,445 --> 00:09:22,029
Of course we have names.

203
00:09:22,613 --> 00:09:24,323
I'm... Lee.

204
00:09:24,407 --> 00:09:26,117
And this is my uncle...

205
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:27,869
Uh, Mushi.

206
00:09:29,245 --> 00:09:31,539
Yes, my nephew was named
after his father,

207
00:09:31,622 --> 00:09:34,083
so just call him Junior.

208
00:09:34,542 --> 00:09:36,252
Mushi and Junior, huh?

209
00:09:36,335 --> 00:09:37,628
My name is Song.

210
00:09:38,212 --> 00:09:40,506
You two look like you
could use a good meal.

211
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:42,049
Why don't you stay for dinner?

212
00:09:42,425 --> 00:09:44,761
Sorry, but we need to be moving on.

213
00:09:44,844 --> 00:09:45,845
That's too bad.

214
00:09:45,928 --> 00:09:48,055
My mom always makes
too much roast duck.

215
00:09:48,139 --> 00:09:49,724
Where do you live exactly?!

216
00:09:52,268 --> 00:09:55,188
Sokka, this is the tenth dead end
you've led us to.

217
00:09:55,438 --> 00:09:58,566
This doesn't make any sense.
We already came through this way.

218
00:09:58,649 --> 00:10:00,485
CHONG: We don't need a map.

219
00:10:00,568 --> 00:10:02,111
We just need love.

220
00:10:02,653 --> 00:10:03,988
The little guy knows it.

221
00:10:04,071 --> 00:10:06,449
Yeah, but I wouldn't mind a map, also.

222
00:10:06,949 --> 00:10:09,410
SOKKA: There's something strange here.

223
00:10:09,494 --> 00:10:11,329
There's only one explanation.

224
00:10:12,413 --> 00:10:13,706
The tunnels are changing.

225
00:10:14,081 --> 00:10:15,750
( RUMBLING )

226
00:10:15,833 --> 00:10:17,627
( CHITTERING )

227
00:10:20,671 --> 00:10:22,465
My daughter tells me you're refugees.

228
00:10:22,799 --> 00:10:25,218
We were once refugees ourselves.

229
00:10:25,468 --> 00:10:29,764
When I was a little girl, the Fire Nation
raided our farming village.

230
00:10:29,847 --> 00:10:32,308
All the men were taken away.

231
00:10:32,391 --> 00:10:34,435
That was the last time I saw my father.

232
00:10:36,145 --> 00:10:38,773
I haven't seen my father
in many years.

233
00:10:39,482 --> 00:10:41,943
Oh. Is he fighting in the war?

234
00:10:45,655 --> 00:10:46,656
Yeah.

235
00:10:52,119 --> 00:10:53,454
CHONG: The tunnels...

236
00:10:53,538 --> 00:10:54,705
They're a-changing.

237
00:10:54,789 --> 00:10:56,415
It must be the curse.

238
00:10:56,499 --> 00:10:59,377
I knew we shouldn't
have come down here.

239
00:10:59,460 --> 00:11:02,255
Right. If only we'd listened to you.

240
00:11:02,338 --> 00:11:04,799
KATARA: Everyone be quiet. Listen!

241
00:11:05,716 --> 00:11:07,385
( WAILING )

242
00:11:14,058 --> 00:11:15,518
( SNARLING )

243
00:11:17,687 --> 00:11:19,689
A giant flying thing with teeth!

244
00:11:21,315 --> 00:11:22,984
No! It's a wolf-bat!

245
00:11:31,367 --> 00:11:33,286
( ROARS )

246
00:11:48,885 --> 00:11:50,136
( GRUNTING )

247
00:11:50,887 --> 00:11:52,013
( SCREAMING )

248
00:12:02,064 --> 00:12:03,983
( GROWLING )

249
00:12:07,194 --> 00:12:09,071
( PANTING )

250
00:12:09,155 --> 00:12:11,407
( SCREAMING )

251
00:12:11,490 --> 00:12:12,742
Yeah, it's no use.

252
00:12:12,825 --> 00:12:13,993
We're separated.

253
00:12:14,243 --> 00:12:16,078
But at least you have us.

254
00:12:16,162 --> 00:12:17,204
( LAUGHS )

255
00:12:17,330 --> 00:12:19,999
( SCREAMS )

256
00:12:29,967 --> 00:12:31,385
Can I join you?

257
00:12:31,469 --> 00:12:33,054
I know what you've been through.

258
00:12:33,137 --> 00:12:35,097
We've all been through it.

259
00:12:35,932 --> 00:12:37,934
The Fire Nation has hurt you.

260
00:12:44,482 --> 00:12:45,942
It's ok.

261
00:12:46,025 --> 00:12:47,568
They've hurt me, too.

262
00:12:53,532 --> 00:12:56,827
( UPBEAT STRUMMING )

263
00:12:56,911 --> 00:12:59,747
♪ Oh, don't let the cave-in
get you down

264
00:13:01,082 --> 00:13:03,167
♪ Don't let the falling rocks

265
00:13:03,250 --> 00:13:05,962
♪ Turn your smile into a frown

266
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:09,006
♪ When the tunnel's at its darkest

267
00:13:09,090 --> 00:13:10,841
♪ That's when you need a clown

268
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,093
♪ Hey

269
00:13:12,927 --> 00:13:17,223
♪ Don't let the cave-in
get you down, Sokka ♪

270
00:13:23,729 --> 00:13:25,106
Aang, look!

271
00:13:25,898 --> 00:13:27,358
AANG: We found the exit!

272
00:13:28,359 --> 00:13:30,069
( STRAINING )

273
00:13:30,152 --> 00:13:32,571
( APPA GROWLS )

274
00:13:36,993 --> 00:13:38,327
( SCREAMING )

275
00:13:49,463 --> 00:13:51,048
This isn't the exit.

276
00:13:51,132 --> 00:13:52,299
No.

277
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:53,968
It's a tomb.

278
00:14:10,484 --> 00:14:12,862
AANG: It must be the two
lovers from the legend.

279
00:14:12,987 --> 00:14:14,363
That's who is buried here.

280
00:14:15,823 --> 00:14:17,867
These pictures tell their story.

281
00:14:27,043 --> 00:14:30,463
KATARA: They met on top of the mountain
that divided their two villages.

282
00:14:32,131 --> 00:14:35,509
The villages were enemies,
so they could not be together.

283
00:14:36,343 --> 00:14:39,055
But their love was strong,
and they found a way.

284
00:14:42,725 --> 00:14:45,478
The two lovers learned earthbending
from the badger-moles.

285
00:14:45,561 --> 00:14:48,064
They became the first earthbenders.

286
00:14:48,147 --> 00:14:51,192
They built elaborate tunnels
so that they could meet secretly.

287
00:14:52,610 --> 00:14:54,111
Anyone who tried to follow them

288
00:14:54,195 --> 00:14:56,072
would be lost forever in the labyrinth.

289
00:14:58,657 --> 00:15:00,743
But one day, the man didn't come.

290
00:15:02,828 --> 00:15:05,289
He died in the war between
their two villages.

291
00:15:08,167 --> 00:15:10,503
Devastated, the woman
unleashed a terrible display

292
00:15:10,586 --> 00:15:12,671
of her earthbending power.

293
00:15:12,755 --> 00:15:14,757
She could have destroyed them all...

294
00:15:16,383 --> 00:15:19,261
But instead she declared the war over.

295
00:15:19,345 --> 00:15:23,224
Both villages helped her build a new city
where they would live together in peace.

296
00:15:25,142 --> 00:15:28,687
The woman's name was Oma,
and the man's name was Shu.

297
00:15:29,688 --> 00:15:31,607
The great city was named Omashu

298
00:15:31,690 --> 00:15:33,692
as a monument to their love.

299
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:42,910
"Love is brightest
in the dark."

300
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:47,998
MOKU: Oh, great!

301
00:15:48,082 --> 00:15:50,334
Your plans have led us
to another dead end.

302
00:15:50,793 --> 00:15:52,711
SOKKA: At least I'm thinking of ideas

303
00:15:52,795 --> 00:15:55,631
and trying to get is out of here, Moku.

304
00:15:56,048 --> 00:15:57,341
Whoa, whoa. Wait a minute.

305
00:15:57,424 --> 00:15:58,717
We're thinking of ideas?

306
00:15:58,801 --> 00:16:01,470
'Cause I've had an idea
for, like, an hour now.

307
00:16:01,554 --> 00:16:02,805
Yes!

308
00:16:02,888 --> 00:16:05,599
We're all thinking of ideas!

309
00:16:05,933 --> 00:16:07,476
Well, then listen to this.

310
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,395
If love is the key out of here,

311
00:16:09,478 --> 00:16:12,481
then all we need to do
is play a love song.

312
00:16:13,065 --> 00:16:15,109
( STRUMMING )

313
00:16:17,111 --> 00:16:19,780
AANG: How are we gonna
find our way out of these tunnels?

314
00:16:19,864 --> 00:16:21,615
I have a crazy idea.

315
00:16:21,699 --> 00:16:22,700
What?

316
00:16:23,159 --> 00:16:25,619
Never mind. It's too crazy.

317
00:16:25,703 --> 00:16:27,079
Katara, what is it?

318
00:16:27,163 --> 00:16:28,455
I was thinking...

319
00:16:28,914 --> 00:16:31,125
The curse says we'll be
trapped in here forever

320
00:16:31,208 --> 00:16:32,585
unless we trust in love.

321
00:16:32,668 --> 00:16:33,961
Right.

322
00:16:34,044 --> 00:16:37,256
And here it says
"love is brightest in the dark"

323
00:16:37,339 --> 00:16:39,675
And has a picture of them kissing.

324
00:16:40,009 --> 00:16:41,468
Where are you going with this?

325
00:16:41,802 --> 00:16:43,387
Well...

326
00:16:43,470 --> 00:16:44,889
What if we kissed?

327
00:16:44,972 --> 00:16:46,599
Us, kissing?

328
00:16:46,682 --> 00:16:49,101
See? It was a crazy idea.

329
00:16:49,185 --> 00:16:50,519
Us...

330
00:16:51,270 --> 00:16:52,271
Kissing.

331
00:16:52,354 --> 00:16:53,355
( SCOFFS )

332
00:16:53,439 --> 00:16:55,983
Us, kissing.
What was I thinking?!

333
00:16:56,066 --> 00:16:57,693
Can you imagine that?

334
00:16:57,776 --> 00:16:59,570
Yeah. ( LAUGHS AWKWARDLY )

335
00:16:59,653 --> 00:17:01,697
I definitely wouldn't want to kiss you.

336
00:17:02,740 --> 00:17:05,743
Oh. Well, I didn't realize
it was such a horrible option.

337
00:17:06,452 --> 00:17:07,912
Sorry I suggested it.

338
00:17:07,995 --> 00:17:09,413
No, no. I mean...

339
00:17:09,496 --> 00:17:12,249
If it was a choice between kissing you
and dying...

340
00:17:12,333 --> 00:17:14,126
- Oh!
- What?!

341
00:17:14,210 --> 00:17:17,755
I'm saying I would rather
kiss you than die. That's a compliment.

342
00:17:17,838 --> 00:17:20,257
Well, I'm not sure
which I would rather do.

343
00:17:21,383 --> 00:17:22,927
What is wrong with me?

344
00:17:24,678 --> 00:17:28,182
( STRUMMING TUNE )

345
00:17:30,267 --> 00:17:32,144
♪ Even if you're lost

346
00:17:32,228 --> 00:17:34,355
♪ You can't lose the love

347
00:17:34,438 --> 00:17:37,358
♪ Because it's in your heart

348
00:17:38,025 --> 00:17:41,195
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

349
00:17:43,405 --> 00:17:44,907
IROH: Thank you for the duck.

350
00:17:44,990 --> 00:17:46,700
It was excellent.

351
00:17:46,784 --> 00:17:47,868
You're welcome.

352
00:17:47,952 --> 00:17:52,039
It brings me joy to see someone
eat my cooking with such gusto.

353
00:17:52,456 --> 00:17:54,083
Much practice.

354
00:17:56,085 --> 00:17:58,128
Junior, where are your manners?

355
00:17:58,254 --> 00:18:01,173
You need to thank these nice people.

356
00:18:01,840 --> 00:18:03,050
Thank you.

357
00:18:03,133 --> 00:18:06,262
SONG: I know you don't think
there's any hope left in the world,

358
00:18:06,345 --> 00:18:07,638
but there is hope.

359
00:18:07,721 --> 00:18:09,306
The Avatar has returned.

360
00:18:10,599 --> 00:18:11,892
I know.

361
00:18:16,772 --> 00:18:18,399
( LOWING )

362
00:18:25,531 --> 00:18:27,032
What are you doing?!

363
00:18:27,116 --> 00:18:30,369
These people just
showed you great kindness.

364
00:18:30,452 --> 00:18:32,746
They're about to show us
a little more kindness.

365
00:18:33,539 --> 00:18:34,540
Well?

366
00:18:50,264 --> 00:18:53,142
AANG: We're gonna run out of light
any second now, aren't we?

367
00:18:53,559 --> 00:18:55,019
I think so.

368
00:18:55,102 --> 00:18:56,395
Then, what are we gonna do?

369
00:18:57,688 --> 00:18:58,897
What can we do?

370
00:19:22,796 --> 00:19:24,923
( STRUMMING )

371
00:19:25,007 --> 00:19:26,592
( GROWLING )

372
00:19:33,432 --> 00:19:34,850
( SNARLING )

373
00:19:38,312 --> 00:19:39,730
( SCREAMING )

374
00:19:43,901 --> 00:19:46,028
CHONG: Hey! You saved us, Sokka!

375
00:19:46,779 --> 00:19:49,448
No. They were trying
to get away from something.

376
00:19:49,823 --> 00:19:50,824
From what?

377
00:19:50,908 --> 00:19:51,909
( RUMBLING )

378
00:19:56,205 --> 00:19:57,790
( GROWLING )

379
00:20:15,682 --> 00:20:16,725
Aagh!

380
00:20:16,809 --> 00:20:17,935
Oof!

381
00:20:21,855 --> 00:20:23,774
( CHORD STRUMS )

382
00:20:29,071 --> 00:20:33,075
( CONTINUES STRUMMING )

383
00:20:33,158 --> 00:20:35,786
Hey, those things are music-lovers!

384
00:20:36,078 --> 00:20:39,164
♪ Badger-moles coming towards me

385
00:20:39,248 --> 00:20:40,290
♪ Come on, guys

386
00:20:40,374 --> 00:20:41,625
♪ Help me out

387
00:20:42,584 --> 00:20:44,795
♪ The big bad badger-moles

388
00:20:44,878 --> 00:20:46,046
♪ Who opened the tunnels

389
00:20:46,130 --> 00:20:47,256
♪ Hate the wolf-bats

390
00:20:47,339 --> 00:20:49,716
♪ But love the sounds ♪

391
00:20:51,051 --> 00:20:53,512
AANG: It's made of some kind of crystals.

392
00:20:53,595 --> 00:20:55,347
They must only light up in the dark.

393
00:20:55,431 --> 00:20:57,433
That's how the two lovers
found each other.

394
00:20:57,516 --> 00:21:00,310
They just put out their lights
and followed the crystals.

395
00:21:02,771 --> 00:21:04,022
That must be the way out!

396
00:21:07,693 --> 00:21:09,069
So, um...

397
00:21:09,153 --> 00:21:10,154
Let's go!

398
00:21:15,701 --> 00:21:16,785
( GROWLS )

399
00:21:29,715 --> 00:21:30,799
What about Sokka?!

400
00:21:31,425 --> 00:21:33,427
( RUMBLING )

401
00:21:35,012 --> 00:21:36,221
( SNARLING )

402
00:21:38,807 --> 00:21:39,808
Sokka!

403
00:21:41,935 --> 00:21:43,395
How did you guys get out?!

404
00:21:43,479 --> 00:21:45,022
Just like the legend says―

405
00:21:45,105 --> 00:21:46,523
We let love lead the way.

406
00:21:46,607 --> 00:21:49,985
Really? We let huge ferocious beasts
lead our way.

407
00:21:51,862 --> 00:21:54,364
( GROWLING )

408
00:21:57,951 --> 00:21:59,578
( CHITTERING )

409
00:22:01,330 --> 00:22:03,081
( ROARS )

410
00:22:06,210 --> 00:22:07,753
Why is your forehead all red?

411
00:22:08,837 --> 00:22:11,840
Nobody react
to what I'm about to tell you.

412
00:22:12,216 --> 00:22:13,634
I think that kid

413
00:22:13,717 --> 00:22:15,427
might be the Avatar.

414
00:22:19,556 --> 00:22:22,017
AANG: So, are you guys
gonna come to Omashu with us?

415
00:22:22,142 --> 00:22:23,685
- Nope.
- Ok.

416
00:22:23,769 --> 00:22:25,103
Thanks for everything, Moku.

417
00:22:27,105 --> 00:22:28,232
Sokka,

418
00:22:28,315 --> 00:22:31,860
I hope you learned a little something
about not letting the plans

419
00:22:31,944 --> 00:22:33,654
get in the way of the journey.

420
00:22:35,739 --> 00:22:37,241
Just play your songs.

421
00:22:37,866 --> 00:22:39,451
Hey! Good plan!

422
00:22:39,576 --> 00:22:41,662
( STRUMMING )

423
00:22:43,497 --> 00:22:45,249
♪ Even if you're lost

424
00:22:45,415 --> 00:22:47,501
♪ You can't lose the love

425
00:22:47,626 --> 00:22:51,255
♪ Because it's in your heart

426
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:55,300
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

427
00:22:56,760 --> 00:22:58,929
SOKKA: The journey
was long and annoying,

428
00:22:59,012 --> 00:23:01,306
but now you get to see
what it's really about―

429
00:23:01,390 --> 00:23:02,933
The destination.

430
00:23:03,141 --> 00:23:04,393
I present to you

431
00:23:04,476 --> 00:23:06,979
the Earth Kingdom city of O―

432
00:23:08,146 --> 00:23:09,731
Oh, no!

433
00:23:21,326 --> 00:23:23,328
( MEN CHANTING RHYTHMICALLY )
